.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH voltkit-resize 1  "Voltkit 0.12.0" "Voltkit Manual"
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH NAME
voltkit\-resize \- Resize pictures in bulk
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBvoltkit resize\fR [\fB\-\-longest\-side\fR] [\fB\-\-percent\fR] [\fB\-\-width\fR] [\fB\-\-height\fR] [\fB\-\-mode\fR] [\fB\-\-enlarge\fR] [\fB\-\-format\fR] [\fB\-\-quality\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIFILE\fR> 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH DESCRIPTION
Each FILE is written to NAME (WxH).EXT beside it; originals are never modified. A picture\*(Aqs own rotation is applied; other metadata is not copied. Choose the size with \-\-longest\-side, \-\-percent, or \-\-width and/or \-\-height (default: \-\-longest\-side 1920). Pictures are not enlarged unless you add \-\-enlarge.
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-longest\-side\fR \fI<PIXELS>\fR
The longest side becomes this many pixels
.TP
\fB\-\-percent\fR \fI<PERCENT>\fR
A share of the original size, in percent
.TP
\fB\-\-width\fR \fI<PIXELS>\fR
At most this wide, in pixels
.TP
\fB\-\-height\fR \fI<PIXELS>\fR
At most this high, in pixels
.TP
\fB\-\-mode\fR \fI<MODE>\fR [default: fit]
How the picture meets \-\-width and \-\-height
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
fit: Keep the shape and fit inside the size
.IP \(bu 2
fill: Keep the shape, fill the size and trim the overflow
.IP \(bu 2
stretch: Exactly the size, even if it distorts the picture
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-enlarge\fR
Allow pictures to be made bigger than they are
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fR \fI<FORMAT>\fR [default: same]
The format to write
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
same: The format of the original
.IP \(bu 2
png
.IP \(bu 2
jpeg
.IP \(bu 2
webp
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-quality\fR \fI<QUALITY>\fR [default: 90]
JPEG and WebP quality from 1 to 100
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIFILE\fR>
Pictures to resize (.png, .jpg/.jpeg, .webp, .gif, .bmp, .tif/.tiff)
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
